proof_profiler_time — implementation plan
==========================================

status: implemented (2026-08-13, experimental)

spec: "profile_proof_time: per-command wall/cpu/gc timing"
(D-2026-08-13-proof-profiler-time). One of three independent profiler
experiments (time / memory / proof-size-delta) built in parallel in
separate worktrees; this plan covers TIME only. Not part of the
wave-numbered rollout in plans/README's index — it is a standalone
ML-registry tool (mcp_tool, plans/ml_builtin_migration's pattern), not
a scala builtin, so it needs no scala-side wiring at all.

advertised metadata (the mcp_tool declaration)
-----------------------------------------------

name          profile_proof_time
description   "Run Isar text against a FRESH, throwaway proof state
              built from the named (already-loaded) theory, and
              report per-command wall/cpu/GC time, slowest first.
              Use this to find which apply/sledgehammer/induction
              step in a proof is slow. This does NOT touch any live
              REPL -- it builds its own state and discards it. If a
              command in the text errors, the report includes every
              command that ran before it (with the failing one
              marked) and stops there; commands after the error never
              ran and are not in the report."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "theory": {"type": "string"},
                 "text": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["theory", "text"]}
annotations   read_only (MCP_Tool.ptyp annotation bucket; no repl_tab
              mutation, no theory-graph mutation -- Theory.begin_theory
              builds a value that is never registered anywhere)
outputSchema  none (single formatted text block, same convention as
              repl_show/repl_text's capture-form tools)

params        theory :: string  "the loaded theory to build the fresh
                                 proof state from (Thy_Info.get_theory
                                 key, e.g. HOL.Main -- same spelling
                                 contract as MCP_Repl's entities/
                                 find_theorems theory param)"
              text :: source    "Isar proof text to run and profile
                                 (source, not string, so it may
                                 contain newlines -- see MCP_Tools.thy
                                 check_value)"

